 save()

 Interview Question

 Q. We never wrote SQL. How is data getting inserted?

 Answer:

 save() is provided by JpaRepository. Spring Data JPA calls Hibernate, and Hibernate generates the appropriate SQL (INSERT or UPDATE) and executes it.

 Flow

 save()
    ↓
 JpaRepository
    ↓
 Hibernate
    ↓
 SQL INSERT
    ↓
 Database

 Interview Questions
 Q. What does save() return?

 It returns the saved entity. If the database generates an ID, the returned object contains that generated ID.

 Q. How does save() know whether to INSERT or UPDATE?

 If the entity's ID is null, Hibernate performs an INSERT. If the ID already exists, it performs an UPDATE.